//? Title: Split a weighted graph with spectral clustering
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en

> Find two communities joined by a weak edge

The graph has six vertices. A, B, and C have strong connections to
each other, as do D, E, and F. A small positive affinity joins C and
D, so all six vertices are in one connected component.

Spectral clustering uses the two smallest eigenvectors of the symmetric
normalized Laplacian. It scales each row of the resulting embedding to
length one, then clusters those rows by k-means. The diagram colors the
original vertices by their fitted labels.

```{cpp, id=spectral-weak-bridge, file="figures/spectral_weak_bridge.svg", results="markdown", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <datamunge/plot/diagram.hpp>
#include <datamunge/stats/spectral_clustering.hpp>

#include <array>
#include <filesystem>
#include <format>
#include <print>
#include <string>

int main() {
    namespace dm = datamunge;
    const dm::linalg::DenseMatrix<double> weights(6, 6, {
         0,  1, .9,  0,   0,  0,
         1,  0, .8,  0,   0,  0,
        .9, .8,  0,.08,   0,  0,
         0,  0,.08,  0, 1.1, .9,
         0,  0,  0,1.1,   0, .7,
         0,  0,  0, .9,  .7,  0,
    });
    const auto fit = dm::stats::fit_spectral_clustering(weights, {.n_clusters = 2, .seed = 121});
    std::println("Connected components {}. Selected eigenvalues {:.5f} and {:.5f}.\n",
        fit.connected_components, fit.eigenvalues[0], fit.eigenvalues[1]);
    std::println("| Vertex | Cluster | Embedding coordinate 1 | Embedding coordinate 2 |");
    std::println("| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: |");

    const std::array<dm::graphics::DiagramPoint, 6> positions{{
        {0, 1.5}, {0, -1.5}, {3, 0}, {7, 0}, {10, 1.5}, {10, -1.5},
    }};
    const std::array<std::string, 6> names{"A", "B", "C", "D", "E", "F"};
    const std::array<dm::graphics::RGB, 2> colors{{{223, 239, 253}, {252, 232, 216}}};
    dm::graphics::Diagram diagram(55, 740);
    dm::graphics::DiagramNodeStyle node;
    node.circle = true;
    node.width = node.height = 1;
    for (std::size_t i = 0; i < names.size(); ++i) {
        node.fill = colors[fit.labels[i]];
        diagram.node(names[i], positions[i], names[i], node);
        std::println("| {} | {} | {:.3f} | {:.3f} |", names[i], fit.labels[i] + 1,
            fit.embedding(i, 0), fit.embedding(i, 1));
    }
    for (std::size_t i = 0; i < names.size(); ++i)
        for (std::size_t j = i + 1; j < names.size(); ++j)
            if (weights(i, j) > 0) {
                const bool across = fit.labels[i] != fit.labels[j];
                dm::graphics::DiagramStroke line;
                line.dashed = across;
                line.width = across ? 1.8 : 2.5;
                diagram.link(names[i], names[j], std::format("{:.2f}", weights(i, j)), line);
            }
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
    diagram.save_svg("build/spectral_weak_bridge.svg");
}
```
// result_begin: markdown
Connected components 1. Selected eigenvalues 0.00000 and 0.02814.

| Vertex | Cluster | Embedding coordinate 1 | Embedding coordinate 2 |
| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: |
| A | 1 | 0.700 | 0.714 |
| B | 1 | 0.700 | 0.714 |
| C | 1 | 0.722 | 0.692 |
| D | 2 | 0.718 | -0.696 |
| E | 2 | 0.701 | -0.713 |
| F | 2 | 0.700 | -0.714 |
\image(figures/spectral_weak_bridge.svg)
// result_end
\caption(Vertex colors show the fitted partition. Edge labels show the original affinity weights.)
\alttext(A, B, and C form one triangle and have the same fitted label. D, E, and F form a second triangle with the other label. A dashed edge with weight 0.08 joins C and D.)

The connected graph has one zero eigenvalue. The next eigenvalue
is about 0.02814, and the second coordinate changes sign across the weak
bridge. The cluster assignments split that bridge and keep each triangle
together.

[Ng, Jordan, and Weiss (2001)|https://papers.nips.cc/paper/2092-on-spectral-clustering-analysis-and-an-algorithm]
